ree ornithine plus cyanamide in water. The main issue is alpha-versus-delta guanidinylation selectivity and the generally slow, catalyst-sensitive nature of cyanamide guanylation of aliphatic amines.']\n\n============================================================\nAddress the above issues in your new network. Do NOT repeat the same mistakes.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"Arginine\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"Prioritize the only route in the supplied literature with experimental continuity to an arginine-specific precursor: the Patel et al. (2015) cyanosulfidic surface branch from acrylonitrile to the arginine alpha-aminonitrile. The graph therefore starts from acrylonitrile as the experimentally defended C3 entry point of that network, then includes both the favored aldehyde-first ordering (34 -> 36 -> 37) and the less favored nitrile-first ordering (34 -> 35 -> 37). Free arginine is reached either by a clearly flagged hydrolysis of intermediate 46 or by a separate late-stage ornithine guanidination route, also flagged as speculative because free-ornithine selectivity in water is unresolved. Disputed direct-arginine claims from HCN polymer hydrolysates are not used as core evidence (Ferris et al., 1973; Ferris et al., 1974).\",\n  \"molecules\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_001\",\n      \"formula\": \"HCN\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"hydrogen cyanide\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_002\",\n      \"formula\": \"NH3\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"azane\",\n      \"common_name\": \"ammonia\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_formed\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mol_003\",\n      \"formula\": \"CH2N2\",\n      \"iupac_name\": \"cyanamide\",\n      \"common_name\": \"cyanamide\",\n      \"inchi\": null,\n      \"role\": \"starting\",\n      \"environment_for